{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivationProperties","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivationProperties","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octDer_annihilates_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octDer_annihilates_one","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationProperties.lean#L48-L50","doc":"The 14 explicit `𝔤₂` derivations all annihilate the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.derivation_annihilates_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.derivation_annihilates_one","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationProperties.lean#L35-L46","doc":"**Every octonion derivation annihilates the identity:** `D 1 = 0`.\n\nThe infinitesimal form of \"an algebra automorphism fixes `1`\"\n(`QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionObstruction.no_fixed_unit`): applying the Leibniz rule to\n`1 = 1·1` gives `D 1 = D 1 + D 1`, so `D 1 = 0`. Consequently every derivation preserves\nthe octonion splitting `𝕆 = ℝ·1 ⊕ Im 𝕆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octMul_one_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octMul_one_right","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationProperties.lean#L31-L33","doc":"`e₀ = Pi.single 0 1` is a right unit for the octonion product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octMul_one_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octMul_one_left","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationProperties.lean#L27-L29","doc":"`e₀ = Pi.single 0 1` is a left unit for the octonion product. ","signatureChunk":0}]}